--- BASELINE REPAIRS (pre-existing integration breakage that blocked the solution-wide gate) ---
The branch HEAD carried two pre-existing defects (integration-merge artifacts) that broke the whole-solution
build/test gate before any NotificationSettings code existed. Both were repaired minimally:
1. Duplicate DrivetrainHealth enum: feature-views/HealthRecommendations/HealthRecommendations.Model.cs declared
   the identical `public enum DrivetrainHealth` TWICE (lines 15 and 97) in namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews
   -> CS0101 -> the App C# compile failed -> no LocalAssembly -> the WinUI XAML markup compiler cascaded
   (WMC0001/WMC0110 "Unknown type 'TsButton'..." + WMC9999 internal NRE, 83 errors). Fix: removed BOTH duplicate
   copies from HealthRecommendations.Model.cs; the surface now relies on the single canonical definition that
   already exists in feature-views/HealthOverview/HealthOverview.Model.cs (whose doc comment documents it as the
   shared definition for both drivetrain-health surfaces). No behaviour change.
2. Corrupt test csproj comment: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had a header comment
   block re-concatenated by prior merges into orphaned prose containing literal Compile/Project markup after a
   premature comment close -> invalid XML (MSB4025) -> dotnet build/test could not load the project. Per the
   file's own documented INVARIANT, consolidated the header back to ONE valid comment + single Project root
   (every previously-linked Compile source preserved), then added this surface's 3 links in sorted position
   (NotificationSettings.Model/Source/ViewModel.cs, between NoVehicleSelected and OverviewTab).

