--- PARITY (web/src/features/settings/components/NotificationSettings.tsx) ---
- Composition: three glass panels reproduced 1:1 —
  (1) Browser/OS Notifications: bell IconBox + title/subtitle; per-permission branch — unsupported message,
      Enable button (default), Enabled badge + "Notify me about" Alerts/Export toggles + hint (granted),
      blocked hint (denied).
  (2) Browser tab signals: "Show unread count" + "Flash tab title on critical alerts" toggles + hint.
  (3) Notification sounds: volume IconBox + title/subtitle; master toggle; autoplay hint (master && !dismissed);
      "Channels" + the 7 channel rows (toggle + Test button, dimmed while master off); volume slider (0-100, step 5).
- Data sources bound via shared P1/S8 seams (no direct HTTP in the view):
  useWebPush -> INotificationPermissionGateway; useNotificationListener -> IWebPushPreferenceStore;
  useSettings/useSaveSettings -> INotificationTabSignalsSource (cache-then-network GET /settings + full-object
  PUT /settings, web `saveSettings.mutate({ ...settings, [key]: value })` parity);
  useNotificationSoundPrefs -> INotificationSoundPreferenceStore; useTranslation -> ILocalizer.
- States: loading (skeleton chrome), loaded, empty (default toggles), stale (chip), offline (cached + chip),
  error (QueryError + retry) all rendered; plus web branches (permission unsupported/default/granted/denied,
  autoplay hint, master-off dimming). tab_badge_enabled/critical_flash_enabled default ON when missing
  (web `settings?.field !== false`). Sound defaults: master off, volume 0.6, web per-channel gates.
- i18n: every SOURCE key resolves through the facade and is present in Strings/en/Resources.resw
  (translation.browserNotifications.*, translation.notificationSounds.* incl. category.*, translation.settings.tab.*).
  testAria interpolates the channel name ("Test {{name}} sound"). The native-only error/freshness chrome keys
  (settings.error.*, settings.staleChip/offlineChip/refresh) carry English fallbacks (the web source has no
  error UI for this surface — same pattern as ChargingDetailSection); common.retry/common.loading are present.
- Telemetry: view.opened slug=NotificationSettings (Loaded), PII-safe (no preference values), per P1/S11.
- A11y: surface Narrator name; every toggle, button and the slider carry AutomationProperties.Name; loading and
  error surfaces are live regions; reduced-motion honoured via the shared chrome.

